//
// Gate E cell: a function declared `-> (S, integer)` answers the synthetic `__tuple<S,integer>` record (`boxed_tuple_return`): its tail's tuple literal is built into a work ref of that record (`synthetic_tuple_return`), and a destructure of the call holds the answer in a `__ref_N`, reads the scalar member and copies the record member into a work ref the place then names.
// @FR-T-Ret: a function returns a `(S, integer)` tuple whole.
// @FR-T-Destr: `(b, c) = pair(7)` binds each member of the returned tuple positionally.
// Prints: 3 4 7 8

struct S { n: integer }
fn pair(k: integer) -> (S, integer) { (S { n: k }, k + 1) }
fn main() {
  t = (S { n: 3 }, 4);
  a = t.0;
  (b, c) = pair(7);
  println("{a.n} {t.1} {b.n} {c}");
}
